{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"15820000c838d75f811b1f43143025ba5ebd3e3fa288cdafda3da2da6106cb76","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_b29ea20c947139db9534e64862315e0179332d9e308ac4b5ee1ed6142f2e8c42","overall_assessment":"The primary policy concern is the violation of double-blind anonymity due to the inclusion of author names, affiliations, and a self-identifying GitHub URL. Data usage is compliant with standard academic practices, and while ethical/impact statements are absent, this is consistent with the 2017 venue norms.","paper_id":"BJ--gPcxl","paper_identity_sha256":"72a7e6c191efcd490fc7364180ad327d97dd23c5e32bf9e782a13e954284a4c5","prompt_identity_sha256":"f243141e71bbc08f8a8a9029173703d457d930ea11cf1625abac367f03931c5d","raw_response_sha256":"cf1d9015e6fc04eb204ad8c9d84def5c6b649d6caba90f31be51394e162a20af","request_identity_sha256":"aed8118054e5a5f26f6985c12cdd5f52190fbbfc9a0543abb73ab100ca55c435","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. While the work focuses on standard image classification benchmarks (STL-10, PASCAL VOC) which are generally low-risk, the lack of discussion regarding the broader ethical implications of generative models (e.g., potential for misuse in creating deceptive content) is a minor omission for a 2017 submission, though not a critical failure given the era and specific application domain.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the STL-10 and PASCAL VOC 2007 datasets. Both are standard, publicly available academic benchmarks. The paper does not explicitly detail the licensing terms or consent mechanisms for these datasets, but their use is standard practice in computer vision research. There is no indication of privacy violations or misuse of restricted data.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Emily Denton, Sam Gross, Rob Fergus) and their institutional affiliations (New York University, Facebook AI Research) on the first page. Additionally, the acknowledgements section mentions specific funding sources (Google Fellowship, CIFAR) and the discussion section provides a direct GitHub URL (https://github.com/edenton/cc-gan) which identifies the lead author. These elements violate double-blind review policies by revealing author identities and affiliations.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-009"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work, including the context-encoder approach of Pathak et al. (2016) and DCGAN (Radford et al., 2016). The authors explicitly distinguish their method from the context-encoder, noting differences in architecture and loss functions. There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the visible text.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a specific 'Broader Impact' statement or checklist, which was not a standard requirement for ICLR 2017 submissions. However, the authors provide a link to their code repository, promoting reproducibility. The absence of a formal impact statement is consistent with the norms of the time but represents a gap in modern compliance standards regarding societal considerations.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"44e7f8137743f917d35679362f82224b5464d20f07fe2289bd1b0f8626e3f58c","paper_id":"BJ--gPcxl","paper_ordinal":17,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"cf1d9015e6fc04eb204ad8c9d84def5c6b649d